# .gitignore is honoured automatically (Prettier 3), so dist/, coverage/ and
# node_modules/ need no entry here.

# Generated by the Lore onboarding tool, not authored in this repo. Its
# onboarding draft is not even valid YAML (a markdown-fenced document in a
# .yml file), which fails `prettier --check` outright rather than merely
# reporting a formatting difference. Issue 189 replaces the draft with a real
# interface; either way the directory's contents belong to that tool, not to
# this repo's formatter.
.lore/

# Verbatim mirrors of re-cinq/lore's eslint plugin rules, byte-compared
# against lore main by scripts/check-lore-plugin-sync.mjs. Formatting them
# here would break byte identity - lore is the format authority. The local
# tools/eslint-plugin-lore/index.mjs is this repo's own and stays formatted.
# Spelled as a file glob, not as the directory: an excluded directory cannot be
# re-included, which would make the negation below unreachable.
tools/eslint-plugin-lore/rules/**/*.mjs

# lore-shared.mjs is this repo's own shim, not a mirror, so it stays formatted.
!tools/eslint-plugin-lore/rules/lib/lore-shared.mjs

# Verbatim mirrors of re-cinq/lore's spec-segmentation and spec-status domain
# libraries, byte-compared against lore main by the same script (decisions 10
# and 11) and kept in lore's own libs/shared/src layout. Formatting them here
# would break byte identity - lore is the format authority. They keep lore's
# `.js` relative imports; scripts/lib/lore-domain-resolve.mjs maps those to the
# .ts files at load time.
tools/lore-shared/
